Z||000000||mrgone||05-23-2001||05:18 PM||||ok im going to try and take my doors apart and try to fix the locks, <P>if i have trouble ill take a diji cam pic and be up here in a flash (no pun intended)<P>im scared||||reg||11
Z||000001||mrgone||05-23-2001||05:40 PM||||ok i just ripped almost all the gromits off the carpet and i cant figure out how to get the window roll up/down handle off||||reg||8
Z||000002||danny boy||05-23-2001||05:55 PM||||There is a little clip behind the round part. the easiest way is to go to the closest parts store and buy a window crank removal tool. or, if you can see it, make a small hook out of something and get behind the crank and pull it out. or use a screw driver and push from the other side.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrgone||05-23-2001||05:59 PM||||ok ill try that<P>whats with all this paper in the door anyway?<P>and what do i do about me ripping off all those white gromits?||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-23-2001||06:37 PM||||THE little clip is shaped like a 'C' and fits in a groove on the shaft. You have to push it off from the open end. make sure it dont pop off to never never land. The paper is supposed to stop drafts thru door handle and window edges. I usually throw them away.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrgone||05-23-2001||06:59 PM||||cool, my bud slid a rag edge behind the handle and yanked, worked perfectly, and i still have the clip<P>the lever that locks / unlocks the door popped off the thing that you put the key into<P>its a rod and a plate with 2 holes in it<BR>should i use twist ties and wire the thing on to there?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||05-23-2001||09:44 PM||||Sounds like you'll need a new clip to hold the linkage on.  Should be able to find one from any junkyard and pretty much any 80's GM car.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrgone||05-23-2001||10:12 PM||||i think a ziptie is a good replacement||||reg||1
Z||000008||cadaver||05-23-2001||11:02 PM||||No a zip tie is not a good replacment. Most parts stores also have these in the HELP section. They have red packages.<BR>DONT THROW AWAY THE PAPER THING. It is called a water shed. And for good reason. It is coated and keeps the water that enters the doors away from the cardboard of the panel. Without it the panel will get trashed.<BR>The HELP section might also have those plastic christmas trees. If you use the right tool they dont break.||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||05-23-2001||11:19 PM||||well maybe, just speaking from own experience. the paper was off my mercedes convertible for 12 years, off my fiero for 4 years. They alway sit out in rain, snow so I can use my shop. Door panels on both are fine. My doors dont fill up with water, theirs drains on the bottom if you keep them cleaned out. Only thing is when its really really cold theres a little freezing draft on my knee by the door handle. I look at the paper as a nuisence, and new cars use plastic sheet with all the goo that gets on everything.||||reg||1
